# Post-agent context gate

Use this **after** you finish implementing, refactoring, or fixing behavior (before ending the turn).

## Did anything move or change?

If **yes** to any below, update docs in the same change (or immediately follow up):

| Change type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| New/changed HTTP routes, schemas, auth behavior | `docs/context/core/SPEC.md`, `docs/context/core/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `src/api/` references |
| New env vars or config keys | `README.md` / `AGENTS.md`, `docs/context/core/SPEC.md`, relevant `config/*.yaml` comments if used |
| New/changed CLI commands | `docs/context/core/SPEC.md`, `docs/context/core/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `AGENTS.md` if user-facing |
| New packages under `src/` or renamed entrypoints | `docs/context/core/SPEC.md`, `docs/context/core/REPO_RULES_FOR_AI.md` file-placement table |
| Retrieval / RAG pipeline stages | `docs/context/core/SPEC.md`, `docs/context/core/ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| New doc file under `docs/context/` | **`docs/context/README.md`** topic table and folder list |

## Cross-check

1. Re-read the sections of **`docs/context/core/SPEC.md`** you would rely on as a new agent — are paths and flows still true?
2. If you changed **where AI should put code**, update **`docs/context/core/REPO_RULES_FOR_AI.md`** placement table.
3. Follow **[update-docs-after-changes.mdc](update-docs-after-changes.mdc)** for README, AGENTS, and topic guides.

If **nothing** architecture- or contract-related changed, note that no doc updates are required.
